{"slug": "scallop-and-fava-bean-salad", "nyt_id": 8504, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/8504-scallop-and-fava-bean-salad", "name": "Scallop and Fava Bean Salad", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "Four servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound fresh fava beans, shelled", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh fava beans", "preparation": "shelled", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 clove garlic, peeled and minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "peeled and minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 pound sea scallops", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "sea scallops", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 teaspoon kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Pinch crushed red pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch crushed red pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ cup fresh lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "fresh lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ cup Italian parsley, chopp", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "italian parsley", "preparation": "chopp", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a medium-size pot of water to a boil. Add the fava beans. When the water returns to a boil, blanch the beans until tender but firm, about 2 to 5 minutes. Drain and refresh under cold running water. Skin the beans and set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat 1 tablespoon of the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Add the garlic and saute for 20 seconds. Add the scallops and sprinkle them with salt, pepper and crushed red pepper. Saute until just cooked through, about 3 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Remove from the heat and toss in the fava beans, lemon juice and parsley. Place in a serving bowl, drizzle the remaining olive oil over the top and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 276.8, "protein_g": 23.1, "carbohydrates_g": 25.9, "fat_g": 11.6, "saturated_fat_g": 1.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 27.2, "sodium_mg": 607.5, "fiber_g": 9.0, "sugar_g": 10.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 9.2, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": ["new year’s day"], "other": ["extra virgin olive oil", "fava bean", "project", "salad", "saute", "scallop", "seafood", "spring"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 6}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1995-05-14", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:20:18.576626+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "scallop-and-halibut-ceviche-salad", "nyt_id": 7752, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/7752-scallop-and-halibut-ceviche-salad", "name": "Scallop-and-Halibut Ceviche Salad", "author": "Jonathan Reynolds", "description": "This recipe came to The Times from Fanny Singer, the daughter of Alice Waters, the chef and food activist. It’s inspired by Ms. Singer’s favorite street food. Ceviche is almost always so astringent that the fish loses identity, but the freshness of the ingredients and softness of the lime marinade here are neither confrontational nor eye-squinching. It’s simple stuff: avocado, grapefruit, prickly chile, cilantro, lime and an absolutely fresh sea creature. Making the dish takes a bit of work, but it’s the perfect recipe for when you don’t want to turn on the stove.", "servings": {"text": "serves 8", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 90, "raw": {"total": "1 1/2 hours"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ¼ pounds fresh sea scallops, sliced in half horizontally and then quartered", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh sea scallops", "preparation": "sliced in half horizontally and then quartered", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ¼ pounds fresh skinless halibut fillet, cut into half-inch cubes", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "fresh skinless halibut fillet", "preparation": "cut into half-inch cubes", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "Sea salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "sea salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 cups lime juice (from about 16 limes)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "lime juice (from about 16 limes)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 to 6 Serrano or jalapeño peppers, halved, seeded and finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": 6.0, "unit": null, "item": "serrano or jalapeño peppers", "preparation": "halved, seeded and finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 medium shallots, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium shallots", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "⅓ cup chopped cilantro leaves, plus more for sprinkling", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped cilantro leaves", "preparation": "plus more for sprinkling", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ cup extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "8 leaves Boston or butter lettuce", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "leaves boston or butter lettuce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 grapefruits (one ruby, one white), peeled and segmented", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "grapefruits (one ruby", "preparation": "one white), peeled and segmented", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 avocados, peeled and thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "avocados", "preparation": "peeled and thinly sliced", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place the scallops and halibut in separate nonreactive bowls. Season each generously with salt. Add ¾ cup lime juice to each bowl, toss again, cover and refrigerate. After 45 minutes, drain the halibut, discarding the lime juice, and return halibut to the bowl. Fifteen minutes later, repeat with the scallops."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Combine the peppers, shallots, cilantro and remaining ½ cup lime juice in a nonreactive bowl, cover and refrigerate."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Fifteen minutes before serving, whisk olive oil into shallot mixture. Pour half over the scallops and half over the halibut. Toss and refrigerate for 15 minutes."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Line each of eight plates with a lettuce leaf. Top with a layer of grapefruit and a layer of avocado. Adjust seasoning of scallops and halibut. Place a handful of each over the avocado slices and sprinkle with cilantro."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 361.9, "protein_g": 24.0, "carbohydrates_g": 19.8, "fat_g": 22.3, "saturated_fat_g": 3.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 51.7, "sodium_mg": 824.2, "fiber_g": 5.1, "sugar_g": 7.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 17.8, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["caribbean", "latin american"], "diet": ["dairy-free", "gluten-free"], "course": ["appetizer", "side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["halibut", "lime juice", "marinate", "scallop", "summer"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/05/23/dining/Scallop-and-Halibut-Ceviche-Salad/Scallop-and-Halibut-Ceviche-Salad-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 64}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2004-11-07", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:09:35.810148+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "scallop-potato-and-bean-ragout", "nyt_id": 11480, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11480-scallop-potato-and-bean-ragout", "name": "Scallop, Potato And Bean Ragout", "author": "Florence Fabricant", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "40 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "½ tablespoon unsalted butter or cooking oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unsalted butter or cooking oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 medium-size onion, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium-size onion", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 small sweet red pepper, cored, seeded and finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small sweet red pepper", "preparation": "cored, seeded and finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 large cloves garlic, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large cloves garlic", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 ounces fresh mushrooms, sliced thin", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "fresh mushrooms", "preparation": "sliced thin", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup dry white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "dry white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 cup hot vegetable stock or water", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "hot vegetable stock or water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 teaspoon fresh thyme leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fresh thyme leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 pound new potatoes, peeled and sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "new potatoes", "preparation": "peeled and sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 cup cooked cannellini beans", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "cooked cannellini beans", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 pint Peconic or Nantucket Bay scallops", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "pint", "item": "peconic or nantucket bay scallops", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 tablespoon finely minced parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "finely minced parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the butter or oil in a heavy three-quart saucepan. Add the onion and sweet red pepper and saute over medium heat until tender. Stir in the garlic, cook another minute or so, then stir in the mushrooms. Stir for about a minute, then add the wine. Simmer gently for five minutes."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Add the stock to the saucepan along with the thyme and the potatoes. Simmer, partly covered, about 15 minutes, until the potato slices are tender."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Briefly rinse and drain the cannellini beans and add them. Simmer another five minutes, then add the scallops. Simmer about five minutes longer, until the scallops are just cooked. Season to taste with salt and pepper and serve, sprinkled with parsley."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 216.8, "protein_g": 8.7, "carbohydrates_g": 37.8, "fat_g": 1.9, "saturated_fat_g": 1.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 5.3, "sodium_mg": 737.4, "fiber_g": 6.6, "sugar_g": 3.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.7, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["gluten-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "potato", "saute", "scallop"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 3.0, "count": 7}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-11-28", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:47:08.923623+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "scallop-salad", "nyt_id": 12657, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12657-scallop-salad", "name": "Scallop Salad", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "This ultrasimple scallop salad, brought to The Times in 2012, comes from Jair Téllez’s restaurant in Mexico City, MeroToro. Easy enough for a weeknight, it requires only a few ingredients. Tender, earthy boiled potatoes complement the quick-seared scallops, while spring onions lend a bit of sharpness.", "servings": {"text": "2 servings", "min": 2, "max": 2, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 spring onions, cut in half", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "spring onions", "preparation": "cut in half", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 tablespoons olive oil, or more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": "or more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 fingerling potatoes, cooked, cooled and cubed", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fingerling potatoes", "preparation": "cooked, cooled and cubed", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 large scallops, sliced in half horizontally", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large scallops", "preparation": "sliced in half horizontally", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 teaspoon sherry vinegar, or more as needed", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sherry vinegar", "preparation": "or more as needed", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "4 cups mixed greens and herbs (sorrel, frisée, arugula, cilantro)", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "mixed greens and herbs (sorrel", "preparation": "frisée, arugula, cilantro)", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Put a dry skillet on medium-high heat. When the skillet is hot, add the spring onions, cut-side down, and cook until charred. Remove from heat, chop and put in a large serving bowl."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Reduce skillet heat to medium; add 1 tablespoon olive oil and the potatoes. Sprinkle with salt and cook until browned; remove and add to the serving bowl."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Keep the skillet on medium heat, and add 1 tablespoon olive oil and the scallops. Sprinkle with salt and pepper, and cook for 1 minute, never turning. Turn off the heat. Add an additional tablespoon olive oil and the sherry vinegar and stir. Add the scallops, cooking liquid and mixed greens and herbs to the bowl with the spring onions and potatoes and toss, adding more olive oil and vinegar as needed. Taste and adjust the seasoning; serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 541.0, "protein_g": 20.2, "carbohydrates_g": 72.9, "fat_g": 27.3, "saturated_fat_g": 5.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 19.2, "sodium_mg": 793.1, "fiber_g": 34.9, "sugar_g": 2.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 18.6, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["easy", "five ingredient", "mixed greens", "potato", "quick", "salad", "saute", "scallop", "seafood"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2012/08/05/magazine/05eat1/05eat1-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 278}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-08-05", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:58:43.242622+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "scallops-and-peppers-with-black-bean-sauce", "nyt_id": 11329, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/11329-scallops-and-peppers-with-black-bean-sauce", "name": "Scallops and Peppers With Black-Bean Sauce", "author": "Marian Burros", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "2 servings", "min": 2, "max": 2, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "16 ounces whole red, yellow or orange peppers, or 14 ounces thinly sliced ready-cut peppers (4 cups)", "group": null, "quantity": 16.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "whole red", "preparation": "yellow or orange peppers, or 14 ounces thinly sliced ready-cut peppers (4 cups)", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 tablespoon canola oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "canola oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons salted black beans", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "salted black beans", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons dry sherry", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "dry sherry", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 clove garlic", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon fresh or frozen ginger", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh or frozen ginger", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "4 scallions", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "10 ounces scallops", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "scallops", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "½ teaspoon sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Wash, trim, seed and thinly slice whole peppers."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Heat oil in a wok or nonstick skillet. Saute peppers in hot oil while preparing the rest of the dish."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Rinse the black beans under running water; then, mash them slightly with one tablespoon of the sherry."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Mince the garlic; grate the ginger; wash, trim and slice scallions."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Add the beans, garlic, ginger and remaining sherry to the peppers, and stir for 10 seconds."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Stir in the scallops. If scallops are small, cook about one minute; cook large ones two or three minutes. Stir in sugar and scallions, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 318.4, "protein_g": 23.4, "carbohydrates_g": 35.9, "fat_g": 8.8, "saturated_fat_g": 0.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 34.0, "sodium_mg": 574.6, "fiber_g": 8.9, "sugar_g": 14.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 7.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["asian"], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["bell pepper", "one pot", "scallop", "stir-fry"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 10}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-05-12", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:02:42.351346+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "scallops-with-leeks-mushrooms-and-potatoes", "nyt_id": 6654, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/6654-scallops-with-leeks-mushrooms-and-potatoes", "name": "Scallops With Leeks, Mushrooms And Potatoes", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "20 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 small red potatoes, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small red potatoes", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Chardonnay, lemon and herb steaming liquid (see recipe)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "chardonnay", "preparation": "lemon and herb steaming liquid (see recipe)", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 medium leeks, white and light green parts only, halved lengthwise and cut across into thin slices", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium leeks", "preparation": "white and light green parts only, halved lengthwise and cut across into thin slices", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 cups shiitake mushrooms, stemmed and thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "shiitake mushrooms", "preparation": "stemmed and thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 pound sea scallops", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "sea scallops", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped Italian parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped italian parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon kosher salt, plus more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "kosher salt", "preparation": "plus more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place the potatoes in a steamer, cover and steam over the liquid for 5 minutes. Add the leeks, mushrooms and scallops and sprinkle with parsley. Steam until the scallops are just cooked through, about 12 minutes. Season with salt and pepper to taste. Divide among 4 plates and serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 263.1, "protein_g": 19.2, "carbohydrates_g": 45.6, "fat_g": 1.5, "saturated_fat_g": 0.4, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 27.2, "sodium_mg": 904.9, "fiber_g": 6.7, "sugar_g": 5.7, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.5, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "dry white wine", "leek", "lemon", "low calorie", "low cholesterol", "sea scallop", "shiitake", "steam", "weeknight"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 3.0, "count": 13}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1995-04-02", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:55:05.069371+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "scallops-with-salad-greens", "nyt_id": 2185, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/2185-scallops-with-salad-greens", "name": "Scallops With Salad Greens", "author": "Craig Claiborne", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 30, "cook_minutes": 10, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "40 minutes", "prep": "30 minutes", "cook": "10 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 pound sea or bay scallops", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "sea or bay scallops", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Salt to taste, if desired", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": "if desired", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "Freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "4 tablespoons olive oil, approximately", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": "approximately", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "¼ pound red leaf lettuce", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "red leaf lettuce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¼ pound corn salad, field salad or mache, available at many greengrocers", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "corn salad", "preparation": "field salad or mache, available at many greengrocers", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 small bunch watercress", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small bunch watercress", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ pound radicchio", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "radicchio", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 tablespoons plus ½ teaspoon balsamic vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "plus ½ teaspoon balsamic vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons butter", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "1 fresh or canned black truffle shaved as thinly as possible, optional", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fresh or canned black truffle shaved as thinly as possible", "preparation": null, "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "If sea scallops are used, cut them crosswise in half. If bay scallops are used, leave them whole. The scallops may be cooked in a skillet or, preferably, on a gas- or wood-fired grill. If they are to be cooked on a grill, preheat the grill until it is quite hot. Sprinkle the scallops with salt and pepper. If they are to be cooked on the grill, rub them all over with 1 tablespoon of oil. Set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "To prepare the lettuce, corn salad, watercress and radicchio, pull off and discard any tough stems and blemished leaves. Rinse and drain thoroughly. Put the greens in a bowl."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Put 3 tablespoons of oil in a mixing bowl, and add the 2 tablespoons vinegar and salt and pepper to taste. Beat thoroughly with a wire whisk. Pour the sauce over the greens and toss."}, {"position": 4, "text": "If the scallops are to be grilled, put them on the grill, and cook briefly about 1 minute or slightly longer. Cooking times will depend on the size of the scallops. Turn the scallops and cook on the second side 1 minute or longer. If the scallops are to be cooked in a skillet, heat 1 tablespoon of oil, and when it is quite hot, add the scallops. Shaking the skillet and stirring, cook for 2 minutes or longer. Do not overcook."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Place the salad greens in an oval or circular serving dish. Arrange the scallops neatly around the greens. Reserve any leftover oil in the skillet."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Heat the butter in a small saucepan until it is hazelnut brown. Do not allow it to blacken. Line a saucepan with a small strainer, and strain in the butter. Stir in the remaining ½ teaspoon vinegar."}, {"position": 7, "text": "Add any leftover oil from the skillet and blend. Spoon this sauce over the scallops. If desired, sprinkle with truffle shavings and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 264.4, "protein_g": 15.6, "carbohydrates_g": 9.2, "fat_g": 18.6, "saturated_fat_g": 4.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 38.7, "sodium_mg": 573.3, "fiber_g": 1.9, "sugar_g": 1.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 13.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": [], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["grill", "saute", "scallop", "seafood", "watercress"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 7}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1988-01-20", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:09:00.100840+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "scandinavian-seafood-salad", "nyt_id": 8496, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/8496-scandinavian-seafood-salad", "name": "Scandinavian Seafood Salad", "author": "Amanda Hesser", "description": "Amanda Hesser", "servings": {"text": "Serves 6", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "1 hour"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "6 fingerling or 2 Yukon Gold potatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "fingerling or 2 yukon gold potatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 cups (about 10 ounces) cooked and peeled small shrimp, cut into small pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(about 10 ounces) cooked and peeled small shrimp", "preparation": "cut into small pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 ½ cups (about 10 ounces) chopped smoked salmon", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(about 10 ounces) chopped smoked salmon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 ½ cups (about 10 ounces) crab meat", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "(about 10 ounces) crab meat", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 hard-boiled eggs, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "hard-boiled eggs", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 shallots, finely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "shallots", "preparation": "finely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 anchovy fillets, chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "anchovy fillets", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped cilantro", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped cilantro", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon sliced chives", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sliced chives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup freshly squeezed lime juice (about 4-5 limes)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "freshly squeezed lime juice (about 4-5 limes)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "3 tablespoons mayonnaise", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "mayonnaise", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "2 tablespoons sour cream", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sour cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Kosher salt and ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "kosher salt and ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "2 small heads iceberg lettuce, separated into leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small heads iceberg lettuce", "preparation": "separated into leaves", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Preheat the oven to 400 degrees. In a small baking dish, roast the potatoes for 30 to 40 minutes, until fork tender. Let cool completely and then peel and cut into ½ -inch dice."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Combine the potatoes with the shrimp, salmon, crab meat, eggs, shallots, anchovies, cilantro and chives in a large bowl. In a small bowl, whisk together the lime juice, mayonnaise and sour cream; fold into the salad and season to taste with salt and pepper."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Arrange the lettuce leaves on a platter and serve alongside the salad. To eat, roll a lettuce leaf around a dollop of salad, like a spring roll."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 339.8, "protein_g": 33.9, "carbohydrates_g": 24.4, "fat_g": 12.2, "saturated_fat_g": 2.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 238.5, "sodium_mg": 966.8, "fiber_g": 4.1, "sugar_g": 5.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 8.4, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["nordic"], "diet": [], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": ["new year’s day"], "other": ["anchovy", "potato", "project", "roast", "salad", "seafood", "spring"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 23}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2006-05-14", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:20:12.192562+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "scrambled-eggs-with-mushrooms", "nyt_id": 1611, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1611-scrambled-eggs-with-mushrooms", "name": "Scrambled Eggs With Mushrooms", "author": "Craig Claiborne, Pierre Franey", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 25, "raw": {"total": "25 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "10 large eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "6 ounces mushrooms, preferably of the wild variety, such as chanterelles, oyster mushrooms, shiitake or morels and so on (if wild mushrooms are not available, the cultivated kind may be used)", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "mushrooms", "preparation": "preferably of the wild variety, such as chanterelles, oyster mushrooms, shiitake or morels and so on (if wild mushrooms are not available, the cultivated kind may be used)", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "10 tablespoons butter", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "butter", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Salt to taste, if desired", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": "if desired", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Freshly ground pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "½ cup finely chopped chives", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped chives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Break the eggs into a mixing bowl. Beat well and set aside."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Place the mushroooms on a flat surface and chop them coarsely into half-inch or slightly smaller cubes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Heat four tablespoons of the butter in a heavy casserole and add the mushrooms. Cook, stirring, about three to five minutes, until they give up their moisture. Continue cooking until the moisture evaporates. Do not brown the mushrooms. The liquid around the mushroom pieces will take on an oily appearance. Remove from the heat and let the bottom of the casserole cool slightly. Place the casserole over moderately low heat and add six tablespoons of the butter, stirring."}, {"position": 4, "text": "When the butter is melted, add the beaten eggs, salt and pepper and start stirring around and around, taking care to scrape the bottom of the casserole all over. If the eggs start sticking to the bottom at any point, the heat is too high. If this happens, remove the casserole from the heat, stirring constantly. Continue cooking over low heat, removing the casserole from the heat as necessary to prevent sticking. The total cooking time is approximately 12 minutes, or slightly longer, until the eggs take on the texture of a very soft custard. Add the chives and stir. Spoon the hot eggs and mushrooms into individual ramekins or small soup bowls and serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 300.7, "protein_g": 11.5, "carbohydrates_g": 3.0, "fat_g": 27.3, "saturated_fat_g": 14.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 360.9, "sodium_mg": 325.0, "fiber_g": 0.9, "sugar_g": 1.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 10.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["vegetarian"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["breakfast"], "occasion": ["new year’s day"], "other": ["egg", "five ingredient", "fry", "winter"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 33}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1986-12-28", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:05:45.710880+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
